                                "text": "1834, Georges Cuvier (baron), Edward Griffith, Charles Hamilton Smith, The animal kingdom arranged in conformity with its organization\nThe naked mollusca are those in which the mantle is simply membranous or fleshy: most frequently, however, it forms in its thickness one or several laminae, of a substance more or less hard, deposited in layers, and increasing in extent, as well as in thickness, because the recent layers always outedge the old ones."
